{
  "_read_me": [
    "This file decides which topic an imported question gets tagged with, which in",
    "turn decides which quiz it can show up in. tools/import_questions.py scores",
    "each question's text against every entry here and picks the best match.",
    "",
    "Scoring: a 'strong' phrase is worth 3 points, a 'weak' phrase 1 point, and a",
    "word from the topic's own name in syllabus.json 0.5 points. Highest total wins.",
    "Below --min-score the question is left unclassified; if the top two topics are",
    "within one point of each other it is flagged ambiguous. Both land in a review",
    "queue rather than being guessed at.",
    "",
    "Keys must be 'subject-slug/topic-slug' and must match content/syllabus.json.",
    "Matching is case-insensitive on word boundaries, so 'sjf' will not fire inside",
    "'sjfoo'. Multi-word phrases match across whitespace.",
    "",
    "This is a keyword classifier, not a language model. Expect roughly three in",
    "four to land correctly on clean text. When one is wrong, add the phrase that",
    "should have caught it to the right topic's 'strong' list - the file is meant",
    "to be edited as you import more papers."
  ],
